# One component per file

Each `.tsx` / `.jsx` file defines **at most one** React component.

- Put additional components in their own file (folder + `index.tsx` is fine).
- Non-component exports (types, constants, context objects, pure helpers) may live in the same file as that single component, or in a sibling `.ts` module when shared.
- **Exception:** TanStack Router route modules may also define the route’s `component` / `shellComponent` function in the same file as the `Route` export. See `.agents/skills/react-component-format/SKILL.md`.

```tsx
// Avoid — two components in ChessBoard/index.tsx
const BoardTilesLayer = () => { ... };
export const ChessBoardFlatMeshes = () => { ... };

// Prefer — BoardTilesLayer/index.tsx + ChessBoard/index.tsx
```
